  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Triple wall – three give-and-gos and a first-time shot",
  "description": "Four lines and a goalkeeper in one half: A and D in the corners by the goal, B and C along the boards out at the defender positions. A has the balls, passes down to B and runs diagonally towards the slot. B plays it straight back, and A passes first time across to C and moves a few metres to the side. C plays it back, A passes first time to D in the corner and moves again, closer to the goal. D plays it back and A shoots first time.\n\nRotation: A goes to B, B to C, C to D and D to A. Also run it mirrored, so that A starts from the other corner. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "A: move after every pass so that you are open for the next return."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Show with your stick where you want the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Passes on target – one bad return stops the whole chain."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "High tempo in the runs, and shoot first time."
    }
  ],
